From afbb94b71bc3d17ad7e889eeed319ed298c7c9ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:27:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/49] Red team fix 2: repack and copy save on the context of
 their workers

The saves of a repack were submitted with the uploader's context, not with
the context of the repack's group of workers. When one worker failed to read
a pack while a save of another worker waited for a free uploader and the
uploads were stalled, nothing cancelled that save: the worker waited for it
and the command hung where upstream returns the read error.

Saves (synchronous and asynchronous) now run on the group context, as
upstream's do. Upstream's saves run inside the workers; here they are
submitted to the uploader's group, which takes the first error returned by
any of its functions. A save given up because the repack was cancelled would
hand that group "context canceled" before the repack returns the read error,
and the command would print the wrong error (10 of 10 runs without this
part). The group context of a repack is therefore marked, and a save that
ends on a cancelled repack context reports nothing to the uploader's group;
its callback still receives the error. Saves of the archiver are untouched.

Test (seat 2 finding 4, carried in, the returned error compared with the
stock control as well): TestRepackReadErrorCancelsQueuedSave hangs before
this commit and returns stock's error after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
